  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has a circular sequence AAA of NNN non-negative integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ where AiA_iAi​ and Ai+1A_{i+1}Ai+1​ are considered adjacent, and elements A1A_1A1​ and ANA_NAN​ are considered adjacent.\n\nAn operation on position ppp in array AAA is defined as replacing ApA_pAp​ by the bitwise OR of elements adjacent to ApA_pAp​. Formally, an operation is defined as:\n\n\nIf p=1p = 1p=1, replace A1A_1A1​ with AN∣A2A_N | A_{2}AN​∣A2​\nIf 1&lt;p&lt;N1 &lt; p &lt; N1&lt;p&lt;N, replace ApA_pAp​ with Ap−1∣Ap+1A_{p-1} | A_{p+1}Ap−1​∣Ap+1​\nIf p=Np = Np=N, replace ANA_NAN​ with AN−1∣A1A_{N-1} | A_1AN−1​∣A1​\nHere, '|' denotes the bitwise OR operation.\n\nNow, Chef must apply operations at each position **exactly once**, but he may apply the operations in any order.\n\nBeing a friend of Chef, you are required to find a sequence of operations, such that after applying all the NNN operations, the bitwise OR of the resulting array is KKK, or determine that no such sequence of operations exist.\n\n###Input:\n\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK denoting the number of elements, and the required bitwise OR after operations.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n###Output:\r\nFor each test case, if no valid sequence of operations exist, print -1.\r\nOtherwise, print NNN space-separated integers in which iii-th integer denote the position chosen in the iii-th operation. If there are multiple valid sequences of operations, you may print any valid sequence.\n\n###Constraints\n\n\n1≤T≤1051 \\le T \\le 10^51≤T≤105\n3≤N≤2∗1053 \\le N \\le 2*10^53≤N≤2∗105\n0≤Ai,K≤1090 \\le A_i, K \\le 10^90≤Ai​,K≤109\nIt's guaranteed that the total length of the arrays in one test file doesn't exceed 10610^6106\n###Sample Input:\n\n`5\r\n3 6\r\n2 1 6\r\n3 6\r\n2 1 5\r\n3 7\r\n2 4 6\r\n3 7\r\n1 2 4\r\n3 7\r\n1 2 6\n`###Sample Output:\n\n`2 1 3\r\n-1\r\n-1\r\n-1\r\n2 3 1\n`Explanation:In the first test case, initially, the sequence is **{2, 1, 6}**.\n\n\nChef applies the operation on the 2nd2^{nd}2nd index, so the sequence converts to **{2, 6, 6}**.\nNext, Chef applies the operation on the 1st1^{st}1st index, so the sequence converts to **{6, 6, 6}**.\nNext, Chef applies the operation on the 3rd3^{rd}3rd index, and this time sequence does not change.\nThe final sequence is **{6, 6, 6}**, and bitwise **OR** of this sequence is 666 that is equal to given KKK.",
